\b The Bible App — Comprehensive User Guide\b0\par
\par
\b Welcome\b0\par
Thank you for using The Bible app. This guide explains every screen and feature so you can get the most out of your experience: reading scripture, journaling, games, favorites, search, settings, widgets, and Live Activities (including Dynamic Island).\par
\par
This guide covers:\par
\tab • Home (Verse of the Day, Timer/Stopwatch/Focus, Resume)\par
\tab • Bible (Books, Chapters, Reader)\par
\tab • Journal (List, Composer/Editor, Smart Links, Tags, Colors)\par
\tab • Favorites\par
\tab • Games (Verse Match, Hangman, Beat the Clock)\par
\tab • Search\par
\tab • Settings\par
\tab • Widgets & Live Activities (Dynamic Island)\par
\tab • Smart Links and inline suggestions (using “**” trigger)\par
\tab • Notifications & Health integrations\par
\par
\b Home Tab\b0\par
\b1. Verse of the Day (or Word of the Night)\b0\par
• The large card shows a daily scripture.\par
• At 6:00 AM and 6:00 PM local time, the verse auto-refreshes.\par
• Tap Refresh (\'ab arrow.clockwise \'bb) to manually load a new verse (disabled when paused).\par
• Tap Copy (\'ab doc.on.doc \'bb) to copy a shareable text like “Book Chapter:Verse — Verse text”.\par
• Tap Share (\'ab square.and.arrow.up \'bb) to share via system share sheet.\par
• Tap the heart to favorite/unfavorite the verse.\par
• Tap anywhere on the verse card to open the Reader at that verse.\par
• Pause/Unpause: Tap the pause icon to freeze the current verse (useful if you want to keep a verse longer). When paused, refresh is disabled, and the verse is mirrored to your widgets.\par
\par
\b2. Prayer/Study Timer\b0\par
• Modes: Timer, Stopwatch, Focus. Use the segmented control to switch modes.\par
\i Timer\i0\par
• Choose a preset (5/10/15/20/30) or tap the slider icon to set a custom duration (1–120 minutes).\par
• While running: Pause/Resume, Stop, and +5 minutes are available.\par
• A local notification alerts you when finished.\par
• Live Activity displays remaining time on the Lock Screen/Dynamic Island.\par
\i Stopwatch\i0\par
• Start, Pause, Stop. Elapsed time appears in a monospaced format.\par
• Live Activity shows running time on the Lock Screen/Dynamic Island.\par
\i Focus\i0\par
• Enter a Title (shown compactly on Live Activity/Dynamic Island). Optionally add a Body.\par
• Tap Save to start/refresh the Focus Live Activity with your content.\par
• Tap Clear to remove Focus content and cancel its Live Activity.\par
\par
\b3. Resume\b0\par
• If you have prior reading progress, the Resume card shows the last place you left off. Tap to jump back into the Reader.\par
\par
\b Bible Tab\b0\par
\b1. Books & Chapters\b0\par
• Navigate by selecting a book, then a chapter.\par
• On iPad, a split interface may be available for larger layouts.\par
\par
\b2. Reader\b0\par
• Read the chapter with verse numbers and text.\par
• Tap a verse row to select and briefly highlight it.\par
• Swipe horizontally to move between chapters (left for next, right for previous).\par
• Long-press a verse to open the quick actions: Copy, Share, Journal, Favorite.\par
\tab – Copy: Copies a formatted verse.\par
\tab – Share: Opens the share sheet.\par
\tab – Journal: Opens the global Journal editor seeded with the reference.\par
\tab – Favorite: Toggles favorite status for that verse.\par
• Progress automatically updates as you read.\par
• “Keep Screen On” (from Settings) prevents the device from sleeping during reading.\par
\par
\b Journal Tab\b0\par
\b1. Journal List\b0\par
• Shows all journal entries (most recent first).\par
• Tap an entry to view details.\par
• Swipe actions:\par
\tab – Trailing (right side): Delete entry.\par
\tab – Leading (left side): Pin/Unpin entry.\par
• Selection Mode: Tap Select to multi-select and bulk delete.\par
• Tag Filters: Tap a tag chip under an entry to filter. Tap “Clear Filters” to reset.\par
• Search: Use the search bar to filter by title, tags, or body text.\par
• New Entry: Tap “New Entry” (square.and.pencil) to open the global editor.\par
\par
\b2. Global Journal Editor (Create or Edit)\b0\par
• The same editor is used everywhere (from the Journal list, Reading view, or entry details).\par
• Title: Enter a title. When opened from a verse, the title may be seeded smartly.\par
• Tags: Enter comma-separated tags (e.g., “sermon notes, prayer, study”).\par
• Tag Colors: On iPad (or when enabled), you can assign colors to tags.\par
• Body: Type your content.\par
• Smart Links:\par
\tab – Type “**” followed by book letters to see a list of Bible books filtered as you type.\par
\tab – Select a book from the suggestions; then type chapter and verse (e.g., “3:16”).\par
\tab – References inside your text are detected and turned into smart links.\par
• Entry Stats & Links:\par
\tab – Shows Word count and Character count.\par
\tab – Lists detected Scripture Links below.\par
\tab – Scripture links appear as blue, underlined text; tap to preview the passage inline.\par
\tab – Copy icon copies the reference text.\par
• Save: Tap Save (square.and.arrow.down) to save your entry.\par
• Cancel: Discards changes and closes the editor.\par
\par
\b3. Journal Entry Details\b0\par
• View a saved entry with title, tags, body, and optional linked verse.\par
• Smart Links in the body are tappable; selecting them shows a preview card inline.\par
• Copy scripture from previews using the copy icon.\par
• Edit (pencil): Opens the same global editor for consistency (with stats/links panel).\par
\par
\b Smart Links — Tips and Trigger\b0\par
• The app automatically linkifies references like “John 3:16” or ranges like “1 John 4:7-8”.\par
• If automatic detection is tricky (e.g., mid-sentence), use the “**” trigger:\par
\tab 1) Type “**”.\par
\tab 2) Start typing a book name; a suggestions list appears.\par
\tab 3) Tap a book to insert it with a space.\par
\tab 4) Type the chapter:verse (e.g., “3:16”).\par
• Detected references become tappable links with blue underline in the editor’s Entry Stats & Links panel and in read-only views.\par
\par
\b Favorites Tab\b0\par
• Shows your favorited verses.\par
• Tap a favorite to open the Reader at that verse.\par
• Swipe to delete a favorite.\par
\par
\b Games Tab\b0\par
\b1. Verse Match\b0\par
• Goal: Choose the verse text that matches the shown reference.\par
• Select verse source (OT/NT/Whole) and difficulty (Easy/Medium/Hard).\par
• Tap Start to begin.\par
• Read the reference and pick the matching text from multiple choices.\par
• After answering, see the correct reference, favorite it if desired, and tap Next.\par
• Stats: Current score, answered, streak, and all-time performance are tracked.\par
\par
\b2. Hangman\b0\par
• Goal: Reveal the hidden word (People, Places, or Books theme).\par
• Pick Theme and Difficulty (Easy: always shows a reference; Medium: after 3 wrong guesses; Hard: only after round ends).\par
• Guess letters using on-screen or hardware keyboard (iPad).\par
• Lives: You have a limited number of mistakes; the word reveals as you guess correctly.\par
• At round end, view the answer and an associated reference (tap to open in Reader).\par
• Stats: Score, answered, streak, and all-time performance are tracked.\par
\par
\b3. Beat the Clock\b0\par
• Goal: Given a person/place label, type a Bible book that mentions it before time runs out.\par
• Choose Category (People/Places/Both) and Difficulty (timer length).\par
• Start and quickly type a book; suggestions appear as you type.\par
• Submit before time expires.\par
• Stats: Score, answered, streak, and all-time performance are tracked.\par
\par
\b Search Tab\b0\par
• Search across books, chapters, or other app areas (depending on the screen).\par
• In Journal, search filters entries by title, tags, or body text.\par
\par
\b Settings Tab\b0\par
• Appearance\par
\tab – Color Scheme: System/Light/Dark.\par
\tab – Font Size: System or a preferred Dynamic Type size.\par
\tab – Font Family: System, Serif, Rounded, Monospaced, or a custom font.\par
• Reading\par
\tab – Reader Font Size: Adjust the size in the Reader views.\par
\tab – Keep Screen On: Prevent the device from sleeping during reading.\par
• Verse of the Day\par
\tab – Scope: Whole Bible, Old Testament, New Testament, or a Specific Book.\par
\tab – Pause Refresh: Freeze the current verse; widgets mirror the frozen verse.\par
• Notifications\par
\tab – Enable alerts for the Prayer/Study timer completion.\par
• Health (if available)\par
\tab – Mindful Minutes logging during Timer/Stopwatch/Focus sessions.\par
\par
\b Widgets\b0\par
• Add the Verse of the Day widget:\par
\tab 1) Long-press the Home screen and tap the + button.\par
\tab 2) Search for “The Bible” widget.\par
\tab 3) Choose a size and tap Add Widget.\par
• The widget mirrors the current Verse of the Day (including paused verses).\par
• The app syncs verse data to the widget via an App Group; updates occur at refresh times or when you manually refresh/pause.\par
\par
\b Live Activities & Dynamic Island\b0\par
• Prayer/Study Timer: Displays remaining time on the Lock Screen and Dynamic Island.\par
• Stopwatch: Displays elapsed time.\par
• Focus: Shows your Title (and optionally Body) on the Lock Screen/Dynamic Island.\par
• Interacting from outside the app:\par
\tab – You can trigger pause/stop/add 5 minutes via shortcut URLs or supported system surfaces.\par
\par
\b Notifications\b0\par
• The app requests notification permission on first launch.\par
• Timer completion triggers a local notification with sound and vibration.\par
• You can disable notifications in system Settings if desired.\par
\par
\b Health Integration (Mindful Minutes)\b0\par
• If Health is available, the app can log mindful sessions during Timer/Stopwatch/Focus.\par
• You’ll be asked for permission on first use.\par
• Logging stops when you stop sessions or leave the app (depending on state).\par
\par
\b Tips & Troubleshooting\b0\par
• Smart Links not detected mid-sentence? Use the “**” trigger to insert a book name intentionally, then type chapter:verse.\par
• Verse of the Day not changing? Check if Pause is enabled. Auto-refresh occurs at 6 AM and 6 PM.\par
• Journal entries missing tags? Enter tags as comma-separated values (e.g., “sermon, prayer”).\par
• Want consistent editing everywhere? The app uses a single global editor sheet for creating and editing entries.\par
• Live Activities not appearing? Ensure notifications and Live Activities are allowed in system Settings, and that a Timer/Stopwatch/Focus session is active.\par
\par
\b Privacy\b0\par
• Your journal entries are stored locally using SwiftData.\par
• Favorites and settings are stored locally.\par
• Health data is only accessed with your permission and only to log mindful minutes.\par
\par
\b Contact & Feedback\b0\par
If you have suggestions or issues, please reach out via the app’s support channel or App Store listing.\par
\par
\b Thank You\b0\par
We hope The Bible app enriches your daily reading, study, and reflection.\par
